From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:46:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(gastown): reconcile queued wisps before pouring in
 deacon and refinery
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The witness recipe collects every queued wisp, keeps one, and burns the
surplus. The deacon and refinery did not, so the three roles converged
differently from the same starting state:

  witness   collect-all + burn-surplus     -> converges from any N
  deacon    --limit=1, no surplus loop     -> sheds one per restart
  refinery  no open-wisp reconcile at all  -> never converges

The refinery is the real defect: every pour site ran `gc bd mol wisp`
unconditionally, so a crash between pour and burn — or any race that
queued two wisps — left an extra wisp that nothing would ever see again.
--limit=1 compounded it on the deacon: even the lookup that exists could
not observe a surplus, so it could not be reported, let alone cleaned up.

Ports the witness pattern to both roles at every pour site:

  OPEN_WISPS=$(gc bd list ... --status=open --type=molecule --include-infra --limit=0 --json | jq -r '.[].id')
  NEXT=$(printf '%s\n' $OPEN_WISPS | sed -n '1p')
  for extra in $(printf '%s\n' $OPEN_WISPS | sed '1d'); do gc bd mol burn "$extra" --force; done
  if [ -z "$NEXT" ]; then  # only pour when nothing is queued
    ...
  fi

Sites:
  agents/deacon/prompt.template.md      no-idle fallback
  agents/refinery/prompt.template.md    lifecycle rules 1 and 2
  formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml       next-iteration
  formulas/mol-refinery-patrol.toml     5 pour sites, incl. the
                                        invalid-existing_pr escalation path

Verified: every `gc bd mol wisp` call in the pack is now behind either an
`if [ -z "$NEXT" ]` guard or the witness's ASSIGNED_WISP equivalent; all
gastown TOML re-parses; `go test ./...` passes.

Refs gc-10x, gc-mgn.

